abstract: >-
  MATLAB scripts that solve Feller's diffusion equation, the Fokker-Planck equation of the Feller process, on the
  half-line, where its diffusion coefficient grows without bound and the support of its solutions may extend to
  infinity. The equation is rewritten in Lagrangian variables, the inverse of the cumulative distribution, so that
  moving nodes carry fixed probabilities and cover the half-line without truncation; the nodes are advanced by ode45.
  The shipped script runs the confining experiment of the accompanying article (Mathematics, 2019).
